title: "evalPriority2Select"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Sekita"
    given-names: "Iwao"
    affiliation: "Visiting Researcher, Faculty of Health Sciences, Tsukuba University of Technology; NPO Shirogame; NPO PCY298"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4215-5003"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sekita/evalPriority2Select"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that takes an evaluation table (`tableE`) and a
  priority table (`tableP`), both written in a heading-based format similar
  to Markdown headings, and outputs a selection tree in the same format for
  conversion into a diagram using `heading2diagram.py`. The tree progressively
  narrows down the available options by evaluating items in priority order.
keywords:
  - evaluation table
  - priority table
  - selection tree
  - heading-based format
  - text-based diagram
